  "_about": "DIPLODOCUS CARNEGII (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05, after Hartman's and Paul's skeletals): 25 m -- a short deep body, the hips higher than the shoulders; a 6.5 m neck held out nearly level, rising a little to a small long low head with a broad square snout; a 12.5 m tail held off the ground, deep at its root and tapering to a whip; columnar legs, the forefeet hoof-like with one thumb claw, the hind with three claws; a row of low keratin spines along the midline. Countershaded drab olive, pale below. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
